{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789291140,"nonce":"8XB1TP8K1SV8tDzD3bSXTk66OfY=","message":"Correction (owner, 2026-09-13): wren_lift needs no change. Its ClassMir\nis already serialisable and already has the foreign form: a class whose\nmethods are ForeignMethodMir stubs (signature, is_static, symbol) with\nno bodies, bound at install through bind_foreign_method_fn. The Wren\nside is therefore:\n\n- caribou-wren builds a ModuleBlob in memory from the registry: one\n  foreign ClassMir per published Haxe class, one ForeignMethodMir per\n  method, getter, setter and constructor (Wren signatures \"hit(_)\",\n  \"hp\", \"hp=(_)\", \"new(_)\", static flags from the interface; symbol =\n  a stable key into the adapter's binding table), class_field_names\n  empty except the one hidden slot, and installs it through the same\n  path a .wlbc takes (interpret_bytecode / install_module_mir).\n- Its bind_foreign_method_fn answers each symbol with a NativeFn that\n  performs the bridge call against the Haxe object in the instance's\n  hidden slot, with the typed Callable resolved once at bind time.\n- resolve_module_fn maps \"game:Player\" to that installed module.\n\nThe wren_lift issue a90a534 filed for a CallBridge instruction is\nwithdrawn and closed. The rest of the previous comment stands: the Haxe\nside is registry-driven HLNative entries plus a build macro emitting\n@:hlNative externs.","files":null}]}